# Every Dockerfile in src/*/ builds with the REPO ROOT as context (services
# read RFQ_ROOT-relative paths like identity/, systems/, authorization/,
# business/, agents/, themes/, interfaces/ -- not just their own src/<service>
# dir + rfq_common). This keeps that broad COPY . /app context lean and
# reproducible -- none of the excluded paths are read at runtime by any
# service, only used for local dev/tooling/tests.
.git
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/uv.lock.tmp
tmp
# BuildKit cache_to export target -- found live: when its DOCKER_BUILDCACHE_DIR
# .env lookup silently missed, this landed a 6.5GB copy at repo root and got
# sent as part of the build context itself (self-inflicted context bloat).
# **/ prefix required -- a bare `.buildcache` only matches at context root,
# NOT infra/.buildcache (found live: that nested copy, ~400MB, kept leaking
# into every service's context after the root-level one was already fixed).
**/.buildcache
# Terraform provider binary caches and state files -- never had a rule here
# at all (only .gitignore had one), found leaking ~95MB combined from
# infra/entra/.terraform + infra/keycloak/terraform/.terraform. State files
# excluded too: not just bloat, they're local dev state that shouldn't ride
# into any image regardless of size.
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup
vendor
node_modules
**/node_modules
skills
docs/vendor
# NOT a blanket `data` exclusion (M8): mission-control-api reads
# data/identity/machine-identity-inventory.yaml at runtime (topology.py).
# data/vendor is NO LONGER excluded (M10, D11): geo-api's Dockerfile bakes
# data/vendor/naturalearth into its own image (~7.8 MB added to every
# service's build context, accepted -- immutable routing inputs belong
# versioned with the code that consumes them, not a separately-managed
# mutable volume). Only data/story remains excluded -- unrelated narrative
# content, never read by any service.
data/story
